   [2m [0m  [1;4mHow bugfix works[0m

      [2m1. [0mThe lead reads the job, finds the files involved, and names who may edit which before anyone starts.
      [2m2. [0mtester writes a test that fails for the bug's own reason. It edits [38;2;177;185;249mtests/[39m only, and reports the failure.
      [2m3. [0mcoder fixes the code so that test passes. It edits only the files the lead named for it, and never [38;2;177;185;249mtests/[39m.
      [2m4. [0mreviewer reads the diff and edits nothing. If it finds a problem, the lead hands it back to coder.
      [2m5. [0mtester runs the whole suite once more, and the lead reports to main.

      [1mWho edits what[0m

      [2m- [0mOne writer per file at a time. Before a member starts, the lead tells it which files are its own.
      [2m- [0mA member that needs a file it does not own asks its owner directly, and tells the lead what they agreed.
      [2m- [0mAnother run of a team may be working in this directory: the leads agree on files among themselves.
      [2m- [0mNobody commits. The person commits.

      [1mReporting[0m

      The lead writes to main when it needs a decision only the person can make, when the job is done, and when it
      cannot be done.
